 ${f}_{x}(x,y)=y{e}^{x}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)={e}^{x}$\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2x{e}^{y+1}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)={x}^{2}{e}^{y+1}$\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=7x-3y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=3x-7y$" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323150 1113 #uuid "3d9883d3-3319-557f-b21a-3239f1c7285f" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323150 1145 "Since the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal, that is, ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y).$ Let's check if this condition is true for each of our pairs of first-order partial derivatives.\n\n- For the first pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x} \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x})={e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the first pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the second pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{e}^{y+1})=2x{e}^{y+1} \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{e}^{y+1})=2x{e}^{y+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the second pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the third pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(7x-3y)=-3 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3x-7y)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the third pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323152 13194139534965 true] [17592186323151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323153 13194139534965 true] [17592186323151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323154 13194139534965 true] [17592186323151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323155 13194139534965 true] [17592186323151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323156 13194139534965 true] [17592186323151 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534965 true] [17592186323151 1041 "selection" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323151 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323155 13194139534965 true] [17592186323151 1110 #uuid "7b9620f6-7875-5312-9df0-897744b0a2e9" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323152 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534965 true] [17592186323152 1111 #uuid "b0157d90-31ad-5d59-85a0-df00192683cf" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323153 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323153 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534965 true] [17592186323153 1111 #uuid "4edf0f67-a3b4-5a61-beb4-abbf38cecb7f" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323154 1034 "I only" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534965 true] [17592186323154 1111 #uuid "2370ec04-0d5e-5ddd-b69f-a42bcffb4665" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323155 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534965 true] [17592186323155 1111 #uuid "73f77b02-25f6-5640-9a2d-ac7bac309a68" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323156 1034 "II only" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323156 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534965 true] [17592186323156 1111 #uuid "3a55f028-8a02-5079-92d4-4667611c3bb2" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323157 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323158 13194139534965 true] [17592186323157 1089 "q-133371" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323157 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534965 true] [17592186323157 1100 "Given that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ evaluate ${f}_{xyx}(1,\\pi )$ if ${f}_{xx}(x,y)={x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).$" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323157 1113 #uuid "4d823fb6-9bd7-5485-9e31-831ff773dec7" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323157 1145 "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyx}(x,y) & ={f}_{xxy}(x,y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{xx}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x{e}^{xy}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+{e}^{xy}\\cdot (-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy))) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{e}^{xy}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\pi ,1):$\n\n$$\n{f}_{xyx}(1,\\pi )={1}^{3}{e}^{1\\cdot \\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot \\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1\\cdot \\pi ))=-{e}^{\\pi }\n$$" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323159 13194139534965 true] [17592186323158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323160 13194139534965 true] [17592186323158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323161 13194139534965 true] [17592186323158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323162 13194139534965 true] [17592186323158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323163 13194139534965 true] [17592186323158 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534965 true] [17592186323158 1041 "selection" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323158 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323159 13194139534965 true] [17592186323158 1110 #uuid "ee5328f6-9e3f-5182-afaf-b21b0795cf6a" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323159 1034 "-{e}^{\\pi }" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323159 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323159 1111 #uuid "4b03206f-42f9-55ab-9959-8ac0a5e1b262" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323160 1034 "{e}^{1-\\pi }" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323160 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323160 1111 #uuid "639b398c-8d54-541c-81e5-b14d4bc840cb" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323161 1034 "{e}^{-\\pi }+1" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323161 1111 #uuid "bd951c22-7641-5b5e-8504-2d807eb5ed42" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323162 1034 "{e}^{\\pi }" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323162 1111 #uuid "201a8ec5-fde0-5565-9518-79e143cf8802" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323163 1034 "1-{e}^{\\pi }" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323163 1111 #uuid "1654d635-99fb-5dd0-9a08-cdc84ebe8e82" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323164 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323165 13194139534965 true] [17592186323164 1089 "q-133382" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323164 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534965 true] [17592186323164 1100 "Suppose that a function $f(x,y,z)$ and all of its higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ and that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}=\\frac{x{e}^{yz}}{x+y},\\,\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂z}=-\\frac{z{e}^{yz}}{x+y}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate the following expression at the point $(1,1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂y∂x∂y}+\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂x∂z}\n$$" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323164 1113 #uuid "efe5e30e-cc66-5eb4-a8f0-4a3803fa0c5b" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323164 1145 "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. \n\nHence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂y∂x∂y} & =\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂x∂{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x{e}^{yz}}{x+y}) \\\\  & ={e}^{yz}\\cdot (\\frac{1\\cdot (x+y)-x\\cdot 1}{(x+y)^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y{e}^{yz}}{(x+y)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn addition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂x∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-\\frac{z{e}^{yz}}{x+y}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x+y}\\cdot ({e}^{yz}+yz{e}^{yz}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{yz}(1+yz)}{x+y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate both partial derivatives at the point $(1,1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂x∂y∂x}{|}_{(1,1,0)} & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{1\\cdot 0}}{(1+1)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂x∂z}{|}_{(1,1,0)} & =-\\frac{{e}^{1\\cdot 0}(1+1\\cdot 0)}{1+1}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂x∂y∂x}{|}_{(1,1,0)}+\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂x∂z}{|}_{(1,1,0)} & =\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323166 13194139534965 true] [17592186323165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323167 13194139534965 true] [17592186323165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323168 13194139534965 true] [17592186323165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323169 13194139534965 true] [17592186323165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323170 13194139534965 true] [17592186323165 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534965 true] [17592186323165 1041 "selection" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323165 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323170 13194139534965 true] [17592186323165 1110 #uuid "1e5a3328-1405-5dcb-9210-3239cf85387d" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323166 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323166 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323166 1111 #uuid "a6a6c7fd-ee6e-59aa-8050-418d17a8235f" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323167 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323167 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323167 1111 #uuid "424466a3-e251-5f36-b488-77274d4cad13" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323168 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323168 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323168 1111 #uuid "3fe0eb88-631a-52a5-b88b-286a16bbfcc7" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323169 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323169 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323169 1111 #uuid "3416353f-2a29-5a6e-a8bd-6916d2fdf14b" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323170 1034 "-\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323170 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323170 1111 #uuid "784765c5-80df-596c-b0a0-95741fad0509" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323171 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323172 13194139534965 true] [17592186323171 1089 "q-133395" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323171 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534965 true] [17592186323171 1100 "Evaluate ${f}_{yzx}(2,1,3)$ given that a function $f(x,y,z)$ and all of its highe