ave ${f}_{xyx}(x,y)={f}_{xxy}(x,y).$ \n\nTherefore, we can swap the order of the subscripts in the first term. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(1,0)+{f}_{xyx}(1,0)-{f}_{xxy}(1,0) & ={f}_{yx}(1,0)+{f}_{xyx}(1,0)-{f}_{xyx}(1,0) \\\\  & ={f}_{yx}(1,0)+\\cancel{{f}_{xxy}(1,0)}-\\cancel{{f}_{xxy}(1,0)} \\\\  & ={f}_{yx}(1,0) \\\\  & =2(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot 0)-(1)^{2}(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1\\cdot 0)+1 \\\\  & =2-0+1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323187 13194139534965 true] [17592186323186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323188 13194139534965 true] [17592186323186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323189 13194139534965 true] [17592186323186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323190 13194139534965 true] [17592186323186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323191 13194139534965 true] [17592186323186 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534965 true] [17592186323186 1041 "selection" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323186 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323187 13194139534965 true] [17592186323186 1110 #uuid "966f789b-7286-527b-8674-40261bb16e30" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323187 1034 "3" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323187 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323187 1111 #uuid "2764a86c-894f-54b7-86a7-f91277cd5125" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323188 1034 "2" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323188 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323188 1111 #uuid "1686b269-6051-5348-a71d-6ef3ecb6efe3" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323189 1034 "1" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323189 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323189 1111 #uuid "2d994160-d5cf-5387-9263-a5c0183ffe32" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323190 1034 "0" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323190 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323190 1111 #uuid "3308199c-8ebd-5baf-8e49-2a5040e1c8fe" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323191 1034 "-1" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323191 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534965 true] [17592186323191 1111 #uuid "b2c21303-b93e-533d-98b4-47f943926a75" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323192 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323193 13194139534965 true] [17592186323192 1089 "q-80643" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323192 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534965 true] [17592186323192 1100 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$, if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =a{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+6xy+2x, \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =b{x}^{3}y+3{x}^{2}+2, \\\\ {f}_{y}(-1,1) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323192 1113 #uuid "ffd78bce-479a-57bc-84cf-9932c814309e" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323192 1145 "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(a{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+6xy+2x) \\\\  & =2a{x}^{2}y+6x+0 \\\\  & =2a{x}^{2}y+6x \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(b{x}^{3}y+3{x}^{2}+2) \\\\  & =3b{x}^{2}y+6x+0 \\\\  & =3b{x}^{2}y+6x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a{x}^{2}y+6x=3b{x}^{2}y+6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of ${x}^{2}y$, we see that $a=\\frac{3b}{2}.$ \n\nNow, since ${f}_{y}(-1,1)=3$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-1,1) & =3 \\\\ b(-1)^{3}(1)+3(-1)^{2}+2 & =3 \\\\ -b+3+2 & =3 \\\\ b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na=\\frac{3b}{2}=3.\n$$" 13194139534965 true] [17592186323193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323194 13194139534965 true] [17592186323193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323195 13194139534965 true] [17592186323193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323196 13194139534965 true] [17592186323193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323197 13194139534965 true] [17592186323193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323198 13194139534965 true] [17592